{"slug":"find-if-path-exists-in-graph","title":"Find if Path Exists in Graph","level":"Easy","summary":"Return whether an undirected graph with n nodes has a path from source to destination.","method":"validPath","params":[["int","n"],["int[][]","edges"],["int","source"],["int","destination"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["3","[[0,1],[1,2],[2,0]]","0","2"],"out":"true"},{"in":["6","[[0,1],[0,2],[3,5],[5,4],[4,3]]","0","5"],"out":"false"},{"in":["1","[]","0","0"],"out":"true"},{"in":["4","[[0,1],[2,3]]","1","0"],"out":"true"}],"lesson":"union-find"},
{"slug":"redundant-connection","title":"Redundant Connection","level":"Medium","summary":"A tree of n nodes (labelled 1..n) had one extra edge added. Return an edge whose removal leaves a tree; if several qualify, the one that appears last in the input.","method":"findRedundantConnection","params":[["int[][]","edges"]],"returns":"int[]","tests":[{"in":["[[1,2],[1,3],[2,3]]"],"out":"[2,3]"},{"in":["[[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[1,4],[1,5]]"],"out":"[1,4]"},{"in":["[[1,2],[2,3],[3,1]]"],"out":"[3,1]"},{"in":["[[3,4],[1,2],[2,4],[3,5],[2,5]]"],"out":"[2,5]"}],"lesson":"union-find","anchor":"redundant-connection--the-edge-that-closes-a-cycle"},
{"slug":"satisfiability-of-equality-equations","title":"Satisfiability of Equality Equations","level":"Medium","summary":"Equations look like \"a==b\" or \"a!=b\" over single-letter variables. Return whether integers can be assigned so every equation holds.","method":"equationsPossible","params":[["String[]","equations"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["[\"a==b\",\"b!=a\"]"],"out":"false"},{"in":["[\"b==a\",\"a==b\"]"],"out":"true"},{"in":["[\"a!=a\"]"],"out":"false"},{"in":["[\"a==b\",\"b==c\",\"a!=c\"]"],"out":"false"},{"in":["[\"a==b\",\"c==d\",\"a!=d\",\"b!=c\"]"],"out":"true"}],"lesson":"union-find","anchor":"satisfiability-of-equality-equations"},
{"slug":"smallest-string-with-swaps","title":"Smallest String With Swaps","level":"Medium","summary":"You may swap the characters at any listed pair of indices, any number of times. Return the lexicographically smallest string you can reach.","method":"smallestStringWithSwaps","params":[["String","s"],["List<List<Integer>>","pairs"]],"returns":"String","tests":[{"in":["\"dcab\"","[[0,3],[1,2]]"],"out":"\"bacd\""},{"in":["\"dcab\"","[[0,3],[1,2],[0,2]]"],"out":"\"abcd\""},{"in":["\"cba\"","[[0,1],[1,2]]"],"out":"\"abc\""},{"in":["\"zxy\"","[]"],"out":"\"zxy\""},{"in":["\"udyyek\"","[[3,3],[3,0],[5,1],[3,1],[3,4],[3,5]]"],"out":"\"deykuy\""},{"in":[],"out":"\"#100002:3bca46cfc6704eb\"","perf":{"label":"a 100,000-character string with 100,000 pairs","gen":"String a0 = BCB.str(100000, \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz\"); List<List<Integer>> a1 = new ArrayList<>(); for (int i = 0; i < 100000; i++) a1.add(Arrays.asList(BCB.rnd(0, 99999), BCB.rnd(0, 99999)));"},"refMs":39}],"lesson":"union-find"},
{"slug":"accounts-merge","title":"Accounts Merge","level":"Medium","summary":"Each account is [name, email…]. Accounts sharing any email belong to the same person. Return the merged accounts as [name, emails in sorted order…]; the accounts themselves may be in any order.","method":"accountsMerge","params":[["List<List<String>>","accounts"]],"returns":"List<List<String>>","check":"any-order","tests":[{"in":["[[\"John\",\"johnsmith@mail.com\",\"john_newyork@mail.com\"],[\"John\",\"johnsmith@mail.com\",\"john00@mail.com\"],[\"Mary\",\"mary@mail.com\"],[\"John\",\"johnnybravo@mail.com\"]]"],"out":"[[\"John\",\"johnnybravo@mail.com\"],[\"John\",\"john00@mail.com\",\"john_newyork@mail.com\",\"johnsmith@mail.com\"],[\"Mary\",\"mary@mail.com\"]]"},{"in":["[[\"Gabe\",\"Gabe0@m.co\",\"Gabe3@m.co\",\"Gabe1@m.co\"],[\"Kevin\",\"Kevin3@m.co\",\"Kevin5@m.co\",\"Kevin0@m.co\"],[\"Ethan\",\"Ethan5@m.co\",\"Ethan4@m.co\",\"Ethan0@m.co\"],[\"Hanzo\",\"Hanzo3@m.co\",\"Hanzo1@m.co\",\"Hanzo0@m.co\"],[\"Fern\",\"Fern5@m.co\",\"Fern1@m.co\",\"Fern0@m.co\"]]"],"out":"[[\"Fern\",\"Fern0@m.co\",\"Fern1@m.co\",\"Fern5@m.co\"],[\"Hanzo\",\"Hanzo0@m.co\",\"Hanzo1@m.co\",\"Hanzo3@m.co\"],[\"Kevin\",\"Kevin0@m.co\",\"Kevin3@m.co\",\"Kevin5@m.co\"],[\"Ethan\",\"Ethan0@m.co\",\"Ethan4@m.co\",\"Ethan5@m.co\"],[\"Gabe\",\"Gabe0@m.co\",\"Gabe1@m.co\",\"Gabe3@m.co\"]]"},{"in":["[[\"A\",\"a@x\",\"b@x\"],[\"A\",\"c@x\"],[\"A\",\"b@x\",\"c@x\"]]"],"out":"[[\"A\",\"a@x\",\"b@x\",\"c@x\"]]"}],"lesson":"union-find"},
{"slug":"min-cost-to-connect-all-points","title":"Min Cost to Connect All Points","level":"Medium","summary":"Connecting two points costs their Manhattan distance. Return the minimum total cost to connect every point (a minimum spanning tree).","method":"minCostConnectPoints","params":[["int[][]","points"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[[0,0],[2,2],[3,10],[5,2],[7,0]]"],"out":"20"},{"in":["[[3,12],[-2,5],[-4,1]]"],"out":"18"},{"in":["[[0,0]]"],"out":"0"},{"in":["[[0,0],[1,1],[1,0],[-1,1]]"],"out":"4"}],"lesson":"union-find"},
{"slug":"regions-cut-by-slashes","title":"Regions Cut By Slashes","level":"Medium","summary":"Each cell of an n×n grid holds \"/\", \"\\\" or a space, cutting the cell. Return how many regions the grid is divided into.","method":"regionsBySlashes","params":[["String[]","grid"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[\" /\",\"/ \"]"],"out":"2"},{"in":["[\" /\",\"  \"]"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[\"/\\\\\",\"\\\\/\"]"],"out":"5"},{"in":["[\" \"]"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[\"//\",\"/ \"]"],"out":"3"}],"lesson":"union-find"},
{"slug":"largest-component-size-by-common-factor","title":"Largest Component Size by Common Factor","level":"Hard","summary":"Values are nodes; two values are connected when they share a factor greater than 1. Return the size of the largest connected component.","method":"largestComponentSize","params":[["int[]","nums"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[4,6,15,35]"],"out":"4"},{"in":["[20,50,9,63]"],"out":"2"},{"in":["[2,3,6,7,4,12,21,39]"],"out":"8"},{"in":["[1]"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[2,3,5,7,11]"],"out":"1"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#5:9d645f34d96218dc\"","perf":{"label":"20,000 values up to 100,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.distinct(20000, 1, 100000);"},"refMs":18}],"lesson":"union-find"}
